ina Faso.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_in_the_Sahel","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"Somalia","extract":"Somalia, officially the Federal Republic of Somalia, is the easternmost country in continental Africa. Stretching across the Horn of Africa, it borders Ethiopia to the west, Djibouti to the northwest, Kenya to the southwest, the Gulf of Aden to the north, and the Indian Ocean to the east. Somalia has the longest coastline on Africa's mainland. Somalia has an estimated population over 19 million, of which 2.7 million live in the capital and largest city, Mogadishu. As one of Africa's most ethnically homogeneous countries, around 85% of its residents are ethnic Somalis. The official and national language of the country is Somali, and Arabic is recognised as a second language. The overwhelming majority of the population are Sunni Muslims.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somalia","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"SO"}],"arc":{"reports":10,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T19:17:58Z","first_title":"As tensions soar in the African horn, Egypt prepares to deploy troops to Somalia","first_url":"https://news.google.?oc=5","first_publisher":"Hiiraan Online","earlier":[{"id":"e_a70f52723680","title":"AU troops to leave 4 bases in Somalia’s Lower Shabelle","date":"2026-10-29T09:09:29Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxPNzdxT0hGaF8yc29NbWhvQWJvcXEyLXNPTVMtOE9sSTNDMEYyNXNfVXowTGJaaGdSbFNtNnR3ZjBTTGt5Ry1PQnNRbHlSWG9OZFprY0p3SXhUYzlTQ05HYjYxQmk0dnA3ZjcyOFVlb0Q1azItTVFja3ZEVFdYdFhQaTQyZDYyWW5nXzktMm43Y3dDQXBvekJxc0xMMkM?oc=5","publisher":"Somali Guardian","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_a75194757979","title":"Uganda withdrawing troops from peacekeeping mission in Somalia","date":"2026-10-31T11:44:28Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxQU3phdUc4ci1Zcl9LdjUzMC1TdnlsZW9RRktORkFLalVXam1KT25tOEJCaE9sbVEtQVlBTUlGU181WGhkUTFnR0lRc2tDNW9tUGtIQ2IxTEFHblo5aFF